-- title:
--   Commutativity of the level-(L,H) Hecke operator family on H¹
-- statement:
--   Fix a set $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$, a commutative ring $\mathcal{O}$, a nonzero natural number $L$, and a subgroup $H$ of $(\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times$. The type [`CohCarrier.Gen L S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) has three families of constructors: a generator $T(\ell)$ for each prime $\ell$ with $\ell \notin S$ and $\ell \nmid L$, a generator $U(q)$ for each prime $q$ dividing $L$, and a generator $\langle d \rangle$ for each unit $d \in (\mathbb{Z}/L)^\times$. The map [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) interprets such generators as $\mathcal{O}$-linear endomorphisms of the cohomology module `H1 L H 𝒪`: both $T(\ell)$ and $U(q)$ are sent to the operator [`CohCarrier.heckeTL`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L23) at the prime in question, which sends a cocycle $\varphi$ to the corestriction of the composite of $\varphi$ with the map induced by `conjL` at that prime, while $\langle d \rangle$ is sent to [`CohCarrier.diamondL`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L55), defined by letting an arbitrarily chosen lift of $d$ to $\Gamma_0(L)$ act through `diamondRaw`. The assertion is that for any two generators $g, h$ of [`CohCarrier.Gen L S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) the associated endomorphisms commute: the product of the operator of $g$ with that of $h$ equals the product taken in the opposite order.
--
--   This is the commutativity of the Hecke algebra generated by the $T_\ell$, the $U_q$ and the diamond operators, realised on the first cohomology of the congruence subgroup of level $L$ cut out by $H$ with coefficients in $\mathcal{O}$. Being uniform in $L$ and $H$, it supplies the commutativity axiom required when a concrete Hecke datum is assembled at any particular level and subgroup, and is used in the subsequent analysis of corner submodules and degree maps.
